!Proposed definitions

;__fi'o__ (FIhO): Converts a selbri into a tag. The tag modifies another selbri by adding a new place to its place structure, corresponding to the first argument of the converted selbri.
;__fe'u__ (FEhU): Terminator for FIhO

!!Formal definitions

||
fi'o ''selbri1'' fe'u ''selbri2'' | lo nu ''selbri2'' cu jai ''selbri1''

fi'o ''selbri1'' ''sumti'' ''selbri2'' | lo nu ''selbri2'' cu jai ''selbri1'' fai ''sumti''

''sentence1'' i fi'o ''selbri'' fe'u bo ''sentence2'' | lo nu ''sentence1'' cu jai ''selbri'' fai lo nu ''sentence2''
||

!!Notes

#fi'o-tags are not currently grammatical as connectors, but other tags are, so the formal definition serves at least as a definition for BAIs as connectors. For example {''sentence1'' iki'ubo ''sentence2''} means {lo nu ''sentence1'' cu jai krinu fai lo nu ''sentence2''}.


